payload.message:
9 more files updated this round. The changes replaced verbose string/collection size idioms with cleaner equivalents:

- **`str != null && str.length() > 0`** → `StringUtils.isNotEmpty(str)` in `AbstractReferenceConfig`, `ReferenceConfigBase`, `Parameters`, `LoggerFactory`, `NetUtils`, and `AbstractConfig`
- **`str.length() > 0`** on known-non-null strings → `!str.isEmpty()` in `AbstractConfig` and `ExtensionLoader`
- **`name.length() == 0`** → `name.isEmpty()` in `ExtensionLoader`
- **`host == null || host.length() == 0`** → `StringUtils.isEmpty(host)` in `NetUtils`
- **`collection.size() > 0`** → `!collection.isEmpty()` in `DubboSpringInitializer` and `ReferenceAnnotationBeanPostProcessor`

